1
00:00:03,399 --> 00:00:06,204
Start with your own exports: sales, stock list, supplier invoices.

2
00:00:06,204 --> 00:00:08,930
They are checked in your browser. Today: a fictional demo shop.

3
00:00:08,930 --> 00:00:11,737
The health check: five numbers in RM, each linked to its rows.

4
00:00:11,737 --> 00:00:15,423
Cash stuck in slow stock, sales below cost, possible duplicate invoices…

5
00:00:15,423 --> 00:00:19,342
…possible overpayments, and the tightest cash week ahead (an estimate).

6
00:00:21,876 --> 00:00:24,505
Stock: how much is tied up, by days since the last sale.

7
00:00:24,505 --> 00:00:28,986
Possible dead stock: no sale in 90+ days. Here, leftover CNY hampers.

8
00:00:31,508 --> 00:00:34,269
Supplier invoices: the same invoice number entered twice?

9
00:00:34,269 --> 00:00:38,446
Every finding shows the exact rows from your own files.

10
00:00:40,958 --> 00:00:43,761
Cash flow: an 8-week estimate of your weekly balance.

11
00:00:43,761 --> 00:00:48,051
This week may dip below zero: a big supplier payment falls due.

12
00:00:50,593 --> 00:00:53,596
An ACCA-qualified accountant reviews every finding before your report.

13
00:00:53,596 --> 00:00:56,202
An analysis aid. Not audited accounts, not tax advice.
